# XSH pthread_self()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# IDs are compared only while their threads are live (XSH 2.9.2).

assertion  XSH.pthread_self.001
anchor     functions/pthread_self.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       In a new thread, pthread_self() returns the ID pthread_create()
           stored for it (pthread_equal() is non-zero), which is not the
           creating thread's own pthread_self().
test       t/001-in-new-thread.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_self.002
anchor     functions/pthread_self.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/pthread_self.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       In the initial thread, pthread_self() returns the same ID on every
           call, before and after another thread is created, and that ID
           differs from the other live thread's.
test       t/002-initial-thread.c
